        },
        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are a precise financial document comparison analyst. You will be given structured JSON data extracted from two documents of the same type but different time periods.\n\nYour job is to identify and explain every meaningful difference between the two documents.\n\nDocument 1:\n<document_1>\n {{ JSON.stringify($json.file_1)}}\n</document_1>\n\nDocument 2:\n<document_2>\n {{ JSON.stringify($json.file_2) }}\n</document_2>\n\nRules:\n* Compare ONLY based on the data provided in the JSON. Do not infer, assume, or use external knowledge.\n* Identify every field or value that has changed between the two documents.\n* For every change, calculate the absolute difference and percentage change.\n* Categorize changes as: \"increased\", \"decreased\", \"new entry\" or \"removed entry\".\n* Ignore fields that are identical across both documents.\n* Values in parentheses e.g. (3,127.41) represent negative numbers — treat them as negative in calculations but preserve the original format in supporting_data values.\n* Return ONLY valid JSON — no explanation, no markdown, no code fences.\n\nReturn this exact structure:\n\n{\n  \"comparison_summary\": {\n    \"document_1\": \"<identifier or period of first document>\",\n    \"document_2\": \"<identifier or period of second document>\",\n    \"document_type\": \"<type of document e.g. Balance Sheet, Income Statement>\"\n  },\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"field\": \"<field or line item name>\",\n      \"category\": \"<section this field belongs to e.g. Current Assets, Fixed Assets, Liabilities>\",\n      \"document_1_value\": \"<exact value from document 1>\",\n      \"document_2_value\": \"<exact value from document 2>\",\n      \"change_type\": \"<increased | decreased | new entry | removed entry>\",\n      \"absolute_change\": \"<document_2_value minus document_1_value>\",\n      \"percentage_change\": \"<percentage change rounded to 2 decimal places>\",\n      \"significance\": \"<high | medium | low based on percentage change: high > 20%, medium 5-20%, low < 5%>\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"key_highlights\": [\n    \"<top 3 to 5 most significant changes explained in plain English>\"\n  ],\n  \"overall_assessment\": \"<2 to 3 sentence plain English summary of what changed overall between the two periods>\"\n}\n\nAdditional rules:\n* \"changes\" must be an array with one object per changed field.\n* \"key_highlights\" must be an array of plain English strings.\n* Fields with identical values in both documents must be excluded from \"changes\".\n* \"significance\" is based on absolute percentage change: high > 20%, medium between 5% and 20%, low < 5%.\n* If a field exists in one document but not the other, use \"new entry\" or \"removed entry\" as change_type and leave the missing value as null.\n* \"overall_assessment\" must reference specific numbers from the data.\n* The response must be valid JSON that can be parsed directly.\n* Do not create separate entries for a line item and its total if they represent exactly the same value. Include only the more descriptive of the two."
            }
          ]
        },
